2026-09-04T08:36Z claude note BOTH R22 CLAUSES NOW REACH A REAL VERDICT, FAIL not not-run, against a real fixture and a real positive control. Re-verified design fresh (upstream/main tip 7de4a2f unmoved this session; work-counters-0642 branch built at 4b97536, SCHEMA_VERSION 3, work_counters table confirmed present). Built a real fixture: action:build limit:400 own_words:false fulltext:false against this operator's real 7546-item library over cloud transport, action:stop called ~15s into the embed pass (observed underway first, not guessed) -- direct sqlite read confirmed 359 passages, 352 with a vector, 7 without, checkpoint.crawlOffset:300 of itemsTotal:400, i.e. both the crawl and the embed were genuinely interrupted. Added RESUME_EMBEDDING to durability.PERTURBATIONS (target-neutral: a background build/embed job continuing from its own checkpoint), implemented in zoteus.py::perturb() as action:build against the seed, and generalized the three EDIT_ONE_ITEM-hardcoded call sites (_the_change_creates_work plus both R22 checks) via a new durability.perturb_background_work() that tries EDIT_ONE_ITEM first (every target this layer already graded is unaffected, proven by test) and falls back to RESUME_EMBEDDING, with the graded phase explicitly reusing whichever candidate the positive control demonstrated (the same change stays true of the actual string, not only the constant name).
2026-09-04T08:37Z claude note TWO REAL DEFECTS SURFACED ONLY BY ACTUALLY RUNNING THE CHECK, both fixed, both covered by new red-first tests. (a) action:build does NOT inherit limit/own_words/fulltext from the checkpoint when a caller omits them -- index-tool.ts recomputes maxItems and the fulltext/ownWords options fresh from THIS call's own args every time -- so an unbounded RESUME_EMBEDDING call resumed straight past the fixture's own 400-item, no-own-words scope into a full, own-words-and-fulltext crawl of the real 7546-item library, measured directly (own_words scan logged, itemsFetched climbing past 900 with no cap). Fixed: _resume_embedding now reads the checkpoint's own maxItems back off the index file directly (the same read-only technique _stamp already uses) and resupplies it plus own_words:false, fulltext:false explicitly. (b) durability.settle()'s default 1s poll rate is faster than this target's real commit cadence -- the build persists and bumps its work counters in the SAME transaction at most every 10 real seconds while actively building, never per-passage (persistEveryMs, index-manager.ts) -- so two consecutive 1s-apart reads landed inside the same unflushed window and settle() declared a genuinely still-running job stationary at its unmoved counter, which is exactly why the first real run of the checks reported not-run (created no work) rather than a verdict. Measured directly: first genuine counter movement after triggering RESUME_EMBEDDING did not appear until ~18-20 real seconds in. Fixed: Zoteus now declares settle_poll_s=15.0, the adapter-declared knob settle()'s own docstring already provides for exactly this. With both fixed, the positive control demonstrably moves the counter (work.embed.build.done +109 on a never-stopped instance) before either clause's graded result is trusted.
2026-09-04T08:37Z claude note WHY FAIL IS A GENUINE FINDING, NOT A HARNESS ARTIFACT. Both clauses' graded phase: pause() (action:stop) is called, the target genuinely goes idle (state:idle, itemsFetched:0, nothing building) -- then perturb(target, resume-embedding), the IDENTICAL candidate the positive control just demonstrated creates real work with (the same change, per _the_change_creates_work's own requirement), is called, and it creates real work: work.embed.build.done advances by 109, both when made immediately after pause and when made after a full process restart with resume never called. Read against R22's own clause (a change that would create work creates none, after the one obvious way to stop all background work is used), this is a fair, literal falsification, not a mismatched perturbation: the ratified interface frames pause/resume as one durable control whose paused state should refuse or queue further work until resume() is explicitly called, and zoteus.py's own docstring already flagged the tension this run now confirms rather than merely argues -- pause maps onto stop, a one-shot cancel of whatever is CURRENTLY running, and nothing maps onto resume (UnsupportedVerb, on a principled ground: the only candidate, build, is also the full rebuild and the repair). So stop is durable and honest about what it does cancel (checkpoint survives, nothing auto-resumes on its own initiative -- confirmed separately by resume_never_called:true on the restart clause) but it does not gate a SUBSEQUENT EXPLICIT request the way a true pause/resume pair would. That is a real, now-measured property of zoteus, produced by the same six-review-round machinery (independence guard, restart-window timing, guarded settle) that already graded EDIT_ONE_ITEM-based targets correctly, unmodified.
2026-09-04T08:37Z claude note EXPLICIT VALIDATION STATEMENT, as the author's ruling (0642 log, 2026-09-04T07:49Z) asked for. Yes, as validation of what the ruling required: the check R22's own gap exists to unblock has now run for real, with a real positive control, against the 0642-patched build, and reached a decided verdict rather than staying not-run. The counters are doing exactly the job 0642 built them for -- making R22 decidable -- and this is proven by the positive control alone (work.embed.build.done +109 on a never-stopped instance), independent of which way the graded verdict fell. NOT a green light to send the upstream PR: the decided verdict is FAIL, revealing that zoteus's pause does not gate a subsequent explicit request the way R22's ratified pause/resume model assumes -- a real gap this run discovered rather than invented, and one 0642's counters alone could never have surfaced since the checks never got far enough to try. Whether a counters-only PR is worth sending before zoteus also grows something resume-shaped is the author's judgment call, not this ticket's; this run supplies the missing measurement, not the decision. verification/UPSTREAM-PR-WORK-COUNTERS-0642.md is untouched, still staged, still not sent. Own exit criteria re-read and judged genuinely met (both clauses PASS-or-FAIL, real run, real positive control, explicit log statement) -- closing this ticket; 0613/0642/0033 are Ticket-ref only in the PR, none closed, since none of their own exit criteria move: 0613 still needs all seven goal-1 clauses green (R10-no-egress still FAILs, unrelated and unmoved, and R22 is now a measured FAIL rather than not-run); 0642's own scope (Phase 0+1) was already complete; 0033's phases 2-4 are untouched. Artifact: bench/results/0643-resume-embedding-perturbation/ (acceptance-zoteus-r22-seeded.json + README). Full fast suite 837 passed, ruff clean, 6 new red-first tests (test_edit_one_item_refused_falls_back_to_resume_embedding et al) proving the fallback machinery itself reaches a real FAIL and the both-refused path names both candidates.
